# Frontend Slop

## Purpose

Agents ship plausible admin UI that **looks wired** while no Go handler ran, styles drift from the single control template, tables truncate instead of sizing columns, errors vanish, or Playwright greens on stubs. This file is the **frontend honesty** catalog. Layout contracts: `ui.mdc` (where not superseded below). General CI lies: `anti-slop.mdc`. Layer map: `frontend-modular.mdc`.

**Operator mandate (2026-09):** no custom one-off styles; one button height; body copy may wrap; headings and numbers must not wrap; table columns width-to-content without ellipsis; no fake `Promise.resolve` stubs; every fetch path surfaces errors. Optional chart preview only: `web/src/domains/dashboards/dashboard_series_mock.ts` when `?chart_mock=1`.

**Binding:** every agent turn that touches `web/**`, admin CI scripts, or OpenAPI cited by admin UI **must** follow **Agent execution protocol** below before claiming done. Subjective praise, abstract "best practices", and unread-file inference are lie modes (`anti-slop.mdc`).

## Agent execution protocol (mandatory)

Agents audit and remediate admin frontend **only** through named catalog IDs in this file, `ui.mdc`, and `scripts/ci/admin/ui_slop.sh`. No generic React/Tailwind advice unless it maps to a specific row below.

### Forbidden output (subjective slop)

| Banned phrase class | Examples | Required instead |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Quality adjectives | "clean", "nice", "elegant", "modern", "polished", "well-structured" | Catalog ID + file:line + falsify command |
| Vague practice | "best practices", "industry standard", "should feel smooth", "good UX" | Contract row: R*, EC*, layout rule, overlay class A/B/C |
| Unfalsified completion | "looks good", "seems wired", "errors handled", "should work" | Tier T1-T2 + proof level L* + pasted command |
| Drive-by praise | "the codebase is in good shape" | Omit or list open catalog hits still in tree |
| Gate fiction | "CI will catch it" without gate name | `bash scripts/ci/admin/ui_slop.sh` or **not run** |

### Mandatory toolchain order

Execute in order; skip a step only when the operator scoped a single file and prior steps already ran in the same turn with pasted output.

| Phase | Tool | Action |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **P0 Scope** | `ls`, `Glob`, `Read` | List touched paths under `web/src/`; read OpenAPI/handler DTO when claiming wire parity |
| **P1 Keyword scan** | `rg` / `grep` | Run rows from **Keyword index** on scope (touched dir or `web/src`) |
| **P2 Classify** | `Read` on hits | Map each hit to **one** catalog ID (EH-*, EC-*, FE-*, ownership class A-J, UX-*, etc.) |
| **P3 Gate** | `bash`, `node --test` | Named gate from **CI gates** when claiming fix; paste command + exit code |
| **P4 Logs** | terminal output, `read_lints` | On failure: paste failing lines; no paraphrase-only "gate failed" |

**Compile ritual ban** (`anti-slop.mdc`): default verification is P1-P4 + `read_lints`; full `npm run typecheck` / `web.sh` only when operator asked or PR claims that gate.

