## State ownership (single writer; semantic race)

**Problem (parallel to BEM + Tailwind on one node):** multiple actors -- components, hooks, `useEffect`, `localStorage` helpers -- **write the same logical object** without one owner. Updates arrive in unpredictable order (user input, fetch resolve, navigation, Strict Mode remount). Symptom: flicker, reverted fields, prefs that "sometimes stick", last-write-wins bugs. This is **not** Go `-race` / shared-memory concurrency; it is **duplicate ownership** in JS.

**Canonical rule:** one logical resource = **one owner** + **one persistence path** + **read-only or callback-only** descendants.

| Logical resource | Owner (canonical) | Children receive |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Directory column prefs | Domain workspace hook (`use_campaigns_directory_workspace`) | `columnPrefs` + `onColumnPrefsChange` only |
| Applied filters / pagination | URL `searchParams` or page hook that owns `setSearchParams` | `draft*` until Apply/submit |
| Server list rows | Fetch hook / page; API is source | `items` down; no client re-filter of full dataset |
| Overlay open (primitive) | Parent **or** internal via `useControllableState` | `open` + `onOpenChange` -- never both fighting |
| Ephemeral drag/resize pixels | Interaction hook/surface only | Commit once via callback on drop/`pointerup` |

Helper: `web/src/lib/controllable_state.ts` (`useControllableState`) for primitives that support controlled + uncontrolled mode.

### Ownership collision classes (never on new/touched code)

| Class | Mechanism | Symptom | Verdict |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **A. Dual React state** | Parent `useState` + child `useState` for same field + `useEffect` sync | Loops, stale closure, lost keystrokes | **Slop** -- lift state or fully controlled child |
| **B. Dual persistence** | Leaf calls `localStorage.setItem` / `save*` AND owner callback persists same key | Prefs diverge after navigation; order-dependent | **Slop** -- persist **only** in owner |
| **C. Uncontrolled mirror** | Child copies `value` prop into local state without `useControllableState` | Drift from parent; "changing props without onChange" | **Slop** -- controlled props or `useControllableState` |
| **D. Sibling writers** | Table + menu + toolbar each call `save*` on same prefs object | Redundant writes; one path skips `setState` | **Slop** -- notify owner once (`onColumnPrefsChange`) |
| **E. Effect vs user input** | `useEffect` resets `draft` from URL/props on every parent render while user edits | Cursor jump; field snaps back | **Slop** -- sync `draft` only on **applied** boundary (Apply, navigation, `listScopeKey`) |
| **F. Dual fetch authority** | Parent passes `items` but child `useMemo` filters/sorts full array | Double filter; wrong totals vs server | **Slop** -- server query params own filter (`cold-path.mdc`) |
| **G. Context + props same field** | `customerId` from Context and from props | Undefined winner | **Slop** -- one source wired at page |
| **H. Optimistic + refetch clash** | Local patch and `onRefresh` both mutate visible row without merge rules | Flash revert or duplicate toast | **Slop** -- one write path until server confirms |
| **I. Ephemeral + committed (allowed)** | Resize: `localWidths` during drag; `columnWidths` from props when idle | Jank if **both** update React state on every `pointermove` | **Allowed** only with handoff guard (`resizeRef` blocks prop sync during drag; commit on `pointerup`) |
| **J. Read-only leaf** | Cell displays `metricsById[id]`; no local copy | -- | **OK** |

### Write path (required shape)

```
Owner (hook / page)
  useState | useReducer  <-- sole React writer
  side effect once       <-- localStorage, setSearchParams, toast after 2xx
       |
       v  props down, callbacks up
Leaves (table, menu, toolbar fields)
  render from props
  onXChange(next)        <-- notify only; NO save*, NO duplicate useState
```

**Banned in leaves:** `saveCampaignListColumnPrefs`, `localStorage.setItem` for keys the owner already owns, second `useState` for the same pref/filter/selection.

### Good patterns

```tsx
// Owner: state + persistence in one place
const [columnPrefs, setColumnPrefs] = useState(() => loadCampaignListColumnPrefs());
const applyColumnPrefs = useCallback((next: CampaignListColumnPrefs) => {
  setColumnPrefs(next);
  saveCampaignListColumnPrefs(next);
}, []);

<Table columnPrefs={columnPrefs} onColumnPrefsChange={applyColumnPrefs} />
<ColumnsMenu columnPrefs={columnPrefs} onColumnPrefsChange={applyColumnPrefs} />

// Leaf: notify only
function onDrop(...) {
  const next = { ...columnPrefs, dataColumnOrder: moveDataColumn(...) };
  onColumnPrefsChange(next); // no saveCampaignListColumnPrefs here
}

// Draft / applied split (filters)
const appliedStatus = searchParams.get('status') ?? '';
const [draftStatus, setDraftStatus] = useState(appliedStatus);
useEffect(() => {
  setDraftStatus(appliedStatus);
}, [appliedStatus]); // boundary: URL applied changed, not every keystroke elsewhere

function onApply() {
  setSearchParams({ status: draftStatus }); // applied owner writes URL once
}

// Primitive controlled / uncontrolled
const [open, setOpen] = useControllableState({
  value: controlledOpen,
  defaultValue: false,
  onChange: onOpenChange,
});

// Ephemeral resize with handoff (use_campaign_list_column_resize.ts)
// - localWidths during pointer capture
// - useEffect skips prop sync when resizeRef.current is set
// - onColumnWidthCommit once on pointerup
```

