## UX scenario contract (one intent, one path, dismissible, scripted)

Agents ship **duplicate entry points** for the same operator intent, **trapped modals**, **silent prerequisite failures**, and **parallel overlays** that fight the same state owner (**State ownership**). This section is the **UX-layer** contract; overlay chrome: `ui.mdc` **Overlays** class C; coalesce: **User action coalescing**.

### 1. One canonical path per intent (per page)

**Intent** = what the operator wants to achieve (create campaign, apply filters, export CSV, archive selection). **Path** = visible control + surface (toolbar button, row menu, dialog).

| Rule | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| **One primary path** | Each intent has exactly **one** primary control in the page chrome (toolbar or page header) |
| **Overflow alternates** | Secondary paths allowed only when **verb + outcome differ** (e.g. **Import** bundle vs **Create** from template) -- not a second unlabeled "Create" |
| **Row vs bulk** | Same mutation: either row action **or** bulk toolbar -- not both without selection guard copy |
| **Footer vs filter row** | Pagination / Apply: one location (`ui.mdc` **Directory filter row**) |
| **Mutex surfaces** | At most **one** class-C overlay (Dialog/Sheet) owning a mutation intent at a time |

**Banned (duplicate intent):**

| Pattern | Why |
| :--- | :--- |
| Same verb, two buttons | "Create" on toolbar + "Create" in empty state + footer without role split |
| Two modals, same POST | Quick-create Dialog + Wizard Sheet both create `campaign` without mutex |
| Hidden duplicate | Command palette route + toolbar button with no shared owner callback |
| Page + global header both Apply same filter | Double fetch / race |

**Campaigns audit (2026-09 -- fix on product decision):**

| Path | Intent label | Verdict |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Toolbar **Create** -> Dialog | Quick create from template | **Primary** |
| More menu **Wizard** -> Sheet | Guided create | **Duplicate intent** with Create until demoted or Create removed |
| More menu **Import** -> Sheet | Migrate / bundle import | **Distinct** intent (different API) |
| Row **Edit** link + bulk **Clone** | Different intents | **OK** with selection rules |

New pages: do not add a second create path without removing or demoting the first.

### 2. Modal dismiss (class C -- required exit vectors)

Applies to `Dialog`, `Sheet`, `CommandDialog` (`components/ui/*`). Operator must never be trapped.

| Vector | Required | Provided by |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **X control** | Yes | `DialogContent` / `SheetContent` built-in (`aria-label="Close"`) |
| **Escape** | Yes | `onKeyDown` on content |
| **Overlay click** | Yes (Dialog); Sheet overlay | `DialogOverlay` / `SheetOverlay` |
| **Labeled Cancel** | Yes for **destructive** or **multi-step** flows | `SecondaryActionButton` -> `onOpenChange(false)` |
| **`onOpenChange(false)`** | Owner clears draft or confirms dirty | Page/workspace hook |

**Minimum bar:** at least **three** of X / Escape / overlay / labeled Cancel on every class-C surface. Destructive confirm (archive, delete): **labeled Cancel required** in footer (`campaigns_directory_overlays.tsx` archive dialog -- OK).

**Banned:**

| Pattern | Verdict |
| :--- | :--- |
| Hand-rolled modal in `domains/` without Escape | **Slop** -- use `Dialog` / `Sheet` |
| `onInteractOutside` / `onEscapeKeyDown` that `preventDefault` with no alternative | Trap |
| Close only via completing mutation | Trap -- always X/Escape/Cancel |
| Stacked class-C modals for same intent | Race + focus trap |

Popover/Select (class B): dismiss via outside click / Escape per `ui.mdc` -- not a substitute for class-C rules.

### 3. Action scripts (sequence + required data)

Every **mutation intent** must have a documented **script**: ordered steps, required fields, server response gates. Source of truth: OpenAPI request body + Go handler validation -- not invented client rules.

**Script table shape (required in PR when adding mutation):**

| Step | User action | Required data (wire) | UI gate | Server success gate |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| n | ... | field names + types | `disabled` / hidden until met | status + response fields |

**Global gates:**

| Gate | Rule |
| :--- | :--- |
| **UUID identity** | Navigate to detail/editor only with `id` from **2xx response** -- never client-generated UUID for persisted entity |
| **Required fields** | Submit `disabled` until OpenAPI-required fields satisfied -- not silent `return` in handler |
| **Optional fields** | Label "Optional" in UI; omit from body when empty |
| **Scope prerequisites** | Missing `customer_id` / license: **disable** primary action or show scope prompt -- not click -> no-op |
| **Success** | Toast / close modal only after `await` 2xx; then owner refresh (**User action coalescing** R2) |
| **Failure** | `ErrorBlock` or inline error -- modal stays open (**Mutation validation** C4) |

**Reference script -- campaigns quick create (`use_campaigns_page.ts` + overlays):**

| Step | Action | Required | UI today |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| 1 | Customer scope | `customer_id` (filter) | Create disabled without scope -- OK |
| 2 | Open dialog | -- | Single `createSectionOpen` |
| 3 | Pick template | `template_id` (UUID) | `createDisabled` without template -- OK |
| 4 | Name | optional string | Labeled optional -- OK |
| 5 | Budget | optional micro int | Validated if present -- OK |
| 6 | Submit | POST body | `creating` guard -- OK |
| 7 | After success | response `id` | `refreshList()` -- must not invent id |

**Violation to fix:** `onCreateCampaign` early `return` when `!customerId || !draftTemplateId` without user-visible error if button were ever enabled -- keep `createDisabled` in sync.

Wizard / import: separate script tables; must not share draft state with quick-create Dialog unless single owner (**State ownership**).

### 4. UX duplicate actors (scenario races)

UX duplicates cause **State ownership** collisions (class A/D) and **coalescing** failures without extra code paths.

| UX duplicate | Scenario race | Mitigation |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Two **Create** entry points | Double POST / two drafts | One primary; mutex `wizardOpen` / `createSectionOpen` |
| Refresh + auto `useResource` dep bump | Abort storm | Coalesce R1; do not also bump token on mount |
| **Apply** + live URL sync on every keystroke | Fight draft/applied | Apply boundary only (`ui.mdc` filters) |
| Toolbar **Pause** + row menu **Pause** | Duplicate bulk API | Shared `onPauseSelected` owner |
| Pagination in footer **and** filter row | Conflicting offset writers | One pagination owner |
| Open overview Sheet + Edit route | Two editors for same row | Close sheet on navigate or single path |
| Double **Export** (toolbar + menu) | Parallel downloads | One handler + `exportBusy` |
| Modal submit + Enter key while loading | Double POST | `loading` disables submit + in-flight guard |

**Mutex rule:** when `creating`, `bulkBusy`, `exportBusy`, or `wizardOpen` is true, disable **conflicting** primary actions on the same page.

### 5. Invalid UX scenarios (catalog)

| ID | Scenario | Symptom | Verdict |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **UX-A** | Visible action always fails | Button -> toast "not available" every time | Remove or wire (`Wizard` toast when callback missing) |
| **UX-B** | Phantom success | Toast before 2xx | **Banned** |
| **UX-C** | Silent no-op | Handler `return` with no UI feedback | **Banned** -- disable control or show scope error |
| **UX-D** | Orphan draft | Close modal; reopen shows stale draft | Reset draft in `onOpenChange(false)` |
| **UX-E** | Competing pagination | Prev/Next in two bands | **Banned** (`ui.mdc`) |
| **UX-F** | Destructive without confirm | Archive/delete immediate | Confirm Dialog with Cancel |
| **UX-G** | Navigate on invented id | `uuid` from counter before POST | **Banned** -- response id only |
| **UX-H** | Two Applies | Filter Apply + auto-apply on change | One Apply submit |
| **UX-I** | Overlay under overlay | Wizard + Create dialog open | Mutex open flags |
| **UX-J** | Error hidden by soft empty | Failed fetch looks like "no rows" | `ErrorBlock` (`Mock lie` / FE2) |
| **UX-K** | Selection action without selection | Bulk enabled with 0 rows | Disable or toast once at click |
| **UX-L** | Long form no Cancel | Sheet wizard multi-step, X only | Add labeled Cancel on step 1+ |
| **UX-M** | Same label, different behavior | Two "Refresh" with different handlers | Rename or merge |
| **UX-N** | E2E proves heading only | Operator thinks flow works | **Test honesty** L1+ |

