## Mutation validation and error contract (fail-closed)

**Principle:** any action that **changes server state** (POST/PATCH/PUT/DELETE, approve, import commit, outbox enqueue) must pass **validation before persistence**. The server is authoritative; the client mirrors validation for UX only and must **surface every failure** to the operator. Silent accept, silent reject, or "happy toast on error" are lies.

Cross-ref: **UX scenario contract** §3 (action scripts), **Wire safety**, `ui.mdc` **Fetch and error UI**, `cold-path.mdc` **Mutation validation**, `pkg/httpresponse`, `web/src/api/client.ts` (`ApiError`).

### Shared wire contract

| Surface | Shape |
| :--- | :--- |
| Success | Handler-specific JSON; status 2xx |
| Failure | `{"error":{"code":"<CODE>","message":"<text>"}}` via `httpresponse.Error` |
| Client parse | `apiFetch` -> `parseApiError` -> `ApiError(status, code, message)` |

Common codes (not exhaustive): `BAD_REQUEST`, `NOT_FOUND`, `CONFLICT`, `FORBIDDEN`, `UNAUTHORIZED`, `LIMIT_EXCEEDED`, `INTERNAL_ERROR`, `APPROVAL_REQUIRED`. OpenAPI documents per-route bodies; handlers use `mapServiceError` / `writeServiceError` (`internal/controlplane/license.go`).

### Server pipeline (mandatory; authoritative)

No mutation handler may **write Postgres / Redis / outbox** until its layer passes. Order:

```
HTTP body -> [size limit] -> [JSON decode] -> [path/auth] -> [domain validate] -> [business rules] -> [TX] -> 2xx
                  |400              |400           |401/403      |400              |409/404/429
```

| Stage | Responsibility | On failure |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **S1. Body limit** | `coldpath.ReadLimitedBody` / `DecodeRequestOrBadRequest` | `400 BAD_REQUEST` -- never read unbounded body |
| **S2. Wire decode** | Typed struct from JSON; path UUID via `ParsePathUUID` | `400` -- malformed JSON or bad UUID |
| **S3. AuthZ / license** | RBAC middleware, license snapshot, tenant scope | `401` / `403` / `LIMIT_EXCEEDED` |
| **S4. Domain validation** | Package `Validate*` functions (shape, ranges, FK refs, flow weights) | `400 BAD_REQUEST` via `validationError` / sentinels |
| **S5. Business invariants** | Budget, revision conflict, approval gates, idempotency | `409 CONFLICT`, `404 NOT_FOUND`, domain codes |
| **S6. Persistence** | sqlc `Queries` inside TX; outbox row same TX when required | Rollback; map DB error -> `mapServiceError` |
| **S7. Response** | `httpresponse.JSON` or `writeServiceError` | Never `200` with error payload; never swallow `err` |

**Banned on server (never ship):**

| ID | Pattern | Why |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **SV1** | `INSERT` / `UPDATE` on raw request fields without S4 | Trusting client |
| **SV2** | `_ = json.Unmarshal` or ignored `DecodeRequest` error | Silent bad input (`anti_slop_gate.sh`) |
| **SV3** | `200 OK` + `{ "error": ... }` in body | Breaks client contract |
| **SV4** | Stack trace or SQL in `message` | Leak; use generic `INTERNAL_ERROR` |
| **SV5** | Validation only in UI; handler passes through | Client bypass |
| **SV6** | Partial TX commit on validation failure | Data corruption |

**Required tests (server):** `mapServiceError` table tests; domain `*_holdout*` / `Validate*_holdout` for non-obvious rules (`TestValidateFlowPathShape_holdout`, `TestBuildCampaignFlowValidateResponse_weightSumUnder100Fails_holdout`). OpenAPI field parity: `TestOpenAPI_*` when adding DTOs.

### Client pipeline (mandatory; operator-facing)

Client validation **reduces round-trips**; it does **not** replace server S4-S5.

```
User submit -> [UI prerequisites] -> [format hints] -> apiFetch -> [ApiError?] -> UI feedback
                    |disable              |inline              |4xx/5xx
```

| Stage | Responsibility | On failure |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **C1. Prerequisites** | Scope (`customer_id`), selection count, modal script (**UX scenario** §3) | Disable submit or scope message -- not silent `return` |
| **C2. Format hints** | JSON parse, positive money, required labels | Inline / `setActionError` before fetch |
| **C3. Transport** | `apiFetch`; `RESOURCE_FETCH_TIMEOUT_MS` | `ApiError` / `TIMEOUT` |
| **C4. Error display** | `ErrorBlock`, modal `actionError`, `userErrorMessage` | Operator sees **code + message** (details in dev only) |
| **C5. Success** | Toast / close modal / navigate with **response `id`** | Only after `await` 2xx (**User action coalescing** R2) |

**Banned on client (never ship):**

| ID | Pattern | Why |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **CV1** | `toast.success` before `await` completes | Phantom success |
| **CV2** | `catch { /* ignore */ }` or `catch { setItems([]) }` | UX-J / silent data loss |
| **CV3** | `console.error` only | Operator blind |
| **CV4** | Client-only validation; server accepts same garbage | SV5 pair |
| **CV5** | `Promise.resolve` fake mutation success | **Fake promises** |
| **CV6** | Generic "Something went wrong" when `ApiError.message` present | Hides server validation text |
| **CV7** | Close modal and discard error on 4xx | Operator loses context |

#### Form patch mapping (**CV-FM**)

Pure `build*PatchBody` / `*ToFormState` mappers in `web/src/domains/**` (no React). Cross-ref: OpenAPI + Go `Patch*Request` decode rules before mapping empty strings.

| ID | Pattern | Why slop | Fix |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **CV-FM1** | Cleared optional UUID sent as `""` on PATCH | Go `uuid.UUID` decode **400**; `null` is no-op | `CLEAR_UUID` (`00000000-…-000000000000`) via `resolveOptionalUuidPatchValue` |
| **CV-FM2** | Invalid numeric form input silently omitted from patch body | Operator thinks value saved (**CV4** pair) | Return `{ ok: false, error }` from mapper before fetch |
| **CV-FM3** | JSON dirty check via raw `form.json !== canonicalJson(snapshot)` | Key reorder false positive; patch or skip wrongly | Parse both sides; `clickQueryParamsEqual` / sorted-key canonical JSON |
| **CV-FM4** | `String(optionalNumber)` equality for dirty check | `0` vs `undefined` drift | Compare `number \| undefined` directly |
| **CV-FM5** | Mandate Zod/Valibot on every form mapper | Stack not in `web/` today; duplicative without shared schema | Manual `parse*` + `*_holdout` tests; schema lib only after explicit stack add |

