## Explicit error handling vs error slop (catalog)

**Explicit error handling** = the operator (or API client) can tell that a request **failed**, sees a **truthful HTTP status**, reads a **safe `error.message`**, and the UI does **not** pretend success. **Error slop** = fake status, stub data, silent swallow, or theater that hides failure.

This section is the **error honesty** catalog. Validation before DB: **Mutation validation and error contract**. Fetch lifecycle: `ui.mdc` **Fetch and error UI**.

### Definitions

| Term | Meaning |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Explicit (server)** | Non-2xx uses `httpresponse.Error`; status matches `mapServiceError`; 5xx logged with `slog.Error`; every handler path writes a response |
| **Explicit (client)** | `apiFetch` failure becomes `ApiError` -> `ErrorBlock` / `StubBanner` / modal `actionError`; no fake empty data |
| **Stub (allowed)** | `StubBanner` / `chart_mock=1` -- **labeled** degraded mode; operator knows data is not live |
| **Stub (slop)** | Empty table, `Promise.resolve([])`, or `genericOk()` **without** banner -- looks like real API success |
| **Fake status** | HTTP 2xx while operation failed, validation rejected, or route unimplemented |
| **Silent swallow** | `catch {}`, `_ = err`, `data ?? []` masking `error` |

### Explicit error handling -- server (required)

| # | Required pattern | Reference |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **ES1** | Decode/body limit fails -> `400` via `DecodeRequestOrBadRequest` / `httpresponse.Error` -- **before** SQL | `pkg/coldpath/http.go` |
| **ES2** | Domain/business failure -> `writeServiceError(w, err)` or mapped `httpresponse.Error` | `license.go` `mapServiceError` |
| **ES3** | Status matches semantics: `400` validation, `404` missing, `409` conflict, `403` RBAC, `401` auth, `5xx` only for unexpected | `TestMapServiceError` |
| **ES4** | Response body on error is **only** `{"error":{"code","message"}}` -- never success DTO mixed with error | `pkg/httpresponse/response.go` |
| **ES5** | `5xx`: operator message generic (`INTERNAL_ERROR`); full `err` in **server logs** only | `writeServiceError` + `slog.Error` |
| **ES6** | Unimplemented/license-gated -> `501` / `403` with clear code -- not `200` empty success | Handler + OpenAPI |
| **ES7** | Handler tests: `httptest` asserts `status` + `error.code` on failure rows | `*_handlers_test.go` |

```go
// Explicit -- map err to truthful status + envelope
if err := svc.Update(ctx, req); err != nil {
    writeServiceError(w, err)
    return
}
httpresponse.JSON(w, http.StatusOK, dto)

// Slop -- never
_ = json.Unmarshal(body, &req)
w.WriteHeader(http.StatusOK)
```

### Explicit error handling -- client (required)

| # | Required pattern | Reference |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **EC1** | `apiFetch`: `if (!response.ok) throw await parseApiError(response)` | `web/src/api/client.ts` |
| **EC2** | List route: `error && !hasSnapshot` -> full-page / section `ErrorBlock` | `campaigns_directory.tsx` |
| **EC3** | `error && hasSnapshot` -> keep rows; toast or inline banner (stale-while-revalidate) | `ui.mdc` |
| **EC4** | Mutation: `catch` -> `setActionError` / `ErrorBlock`; **modal stays open** on 4xx | `campaigns_directory_overlays.tsx` |
| **EC5** | Success toast / close / navigate **only after** `await` 2xx | **User action coalescing** CV1 |
| **EC6** | `501` / license / forbidden: `StubBanner` with **server `message`** -- explicit stub | `campaign_wizard_panel.tsx` `panelError` |
| **EC7** | `userErrorMessage(err)` surfaces `ApiError.message`; technical details via `shouldShowAdminErrorDetails()` in local dev only | `admin_error.ts` |
| **EC8** | `isAbortError` -> no error UI (cancelled fetch is not a failure) | `client.ts` |
| **EC9** | Missing prerequisite (no `customer_id`): disable or scope prompt -- not fake `[]` fetch | **Fake promises** |

```tsx
// Explicit
try {
  await createSelfServeCampaign(body);
  toast.success('Campaign created');
  onClose();
} catch (err) {
  setActionError(err instanceof Error ? err : new Error(String(err)));
}

// Slop -- never
try {
  await createSelfServeCampaign(body);
} catch {
  setItems([]);
}
toast.success('Campaign created');
```

### Error slop catalog (never ship; never cite as "handled")

#### Fake HTTP status (**EH-F**)

| ID | Pattern | Why slop | Explicit alternative |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **EH-F1** | `200 OK` on validation failure | Client assumes success | `400 BAD_REQUEST` + envelope |
| **EH-F2** | `genericOk()` / `{ status: 'ok' }` on unimplemented mutation | Fake save in client or handler | `404`/`501` or real handler + live round-trip |
| **EH-F3** | `200` + empty list to avoid error UI | Hides `500` | Truthful status + `ErrorBlock` |
| **EH-F4** | `500` for known validation (`validationError`) | Wrong semantics | `400` via `mapServiceError` |
| **EH-F5** | `2xx` after TX rollback / partial write | Data lie | Rollback + `409`/`500` |

#### Stub without disclosure (**EH-ST**)

| ID | Pattern | Why slop | Explicit alternative |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **EH-ST1** | `Promise.resolve([])` / `{ items: [], total: 0 }` on guard fail | Fake empty API | `undefined` + scope UI / `EmptyState` |
| **EH-ST2** | `data ?? []` when fetch errored or shape wrong | Masks `TypeError` / error | `Array.isArray` in `*_api.ts`; show `ErrorBlock` |
| **EH-ST3** | Chart/dashboard synthetic fill on T1 without `chart_mock=1` | Silent KPI fiction | Empty charts or labeled `chart_mock` preview |
| **EH-ST4** | `501` route renders blank main | Operator thinks "no data" | `StubBanner` with server message |
| **EH-ST5** | `EmptyState` when `error && !hasSnapshot` | Confuses error with zero rows | `ErrorBlock` |

#### Silent swallow (**EH-SI**)

| ID | Pattern | Why slop | Explicit alternative |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **EH-SI1** | `catch {}` / `catch { return }` in mutation or fetch | Operator blind | EC4 / EC2 |
| **EH-SI2** | `catch { setItems([]) }` | **EH-ST1** + data wipe | EC2 |
| **EH-SI3** | `console.error` only | Not operator-visible | `ErrorBlock` / toast error |
| **EH-SI4** | `_ = json.Unmarshal`, `_ = w.Write` in handlers | `anti_slop_gate.sh` | Return `writeServiceError` |
