## Directory tables (markup, lifecycle, performance)

Applies to all admin lists: `DirectoryTable` / `OpsTable`, campaigns directory, customers, click log, ops DLQ, etc. Scroll and chrome: `ui.mdc` (**Data tables**). Reference (column reorder + resize): `web/src/domains/campaigns/list/campaigns_list_table.tsx`.

### DOM model (required shape)

| Layer | Markup | Role |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Scroll shell | `DirectoryTable` wrap or campaigns table surface const | `overflow-x-auto`; sticky `thead` in scrollable campaigns wrap |
| Column widths | `<colgroup><col /></colgroup>` | One `col` per logical column; width from probe or user commit |
| Header | `<thead><tr><th>` per column | Sort, drag grip, resize separator -- **header-only** interaction state |
| Body | `<tbody>` + one `<tr>` per server row | `columns.map(columnId => <td key={columnId}>)` -- cell order follows prefs, not row data |
| Footer | `<tfoot>` optional totals row | Same `columns` order as header |

**Row/column lifecycle:** column order and width live in **prefs** (`columnPrefs`, localStorage) or server query -- not inside row DTOs. **Single owner:** workspace hook writes prefs; table/menu/toolbar call `onColumnPrefsChange` only (`frontend-slop.mdc` **State ownership**). Each body row is `items[i]`; each cell reads `columnId` and picks field/metric from maps (`metricsById`, `customerNameById`). Reorder permutes `<td>` nodes inside each `<tr>`; React `key={columnId}` preserves cell instances across permute.

**Banned:** CSS `display: grid` / flex matrices pretending to be data tables; bespoke row factories that hide column identity; row keys that change on column reorder. Decision table: **Layout contract** above.

### Scroll variants

| Variant | Wrap | Table width | Header |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Dense directory** (campaigns, wide metrics) | Scrollable; `flex: 1; min-height: 0` | `width: auto` (sum of columns) | Sticky inside wrap |
| **Ops / small directory** | Static wrap; clip radius | `width: 100%` | Not sticky |

### Good patterns (required for new / touched tables)

| Pattern | Why |
| :--- | :--- |
| Semantic `<table>`, `DirectoryTable` or `OpsTable` | One scroll contract; `ui_slop.sh` bans raw `<table>` in domains |
| `key={columnId}` on `<td>` / `<th>` | Safe column reorder without remounting row identity |
| `key={row.id}` on `<tr>` | Stable row across column permute and pagination |
| Row VM in `useMemo` (`buildCampaignRowVm` pattern) | Format once per row per data change, not per header paint |
| `React.memo` on body row component | Parent header/drag state must not reconcile N rows |
| Column resize: mutate `<col>` / CSS var via **ref** during pointermove; commit width to React state on `pointerup` only | Avoids full-table React + layout on every pixel |
| Column drag highlight: state or `data-*` on **header row only** | `dragover` must not lift state to component that owns `<tbody>` |
| `requestAnimationFrame` throttle on pointermove / dragover handlers | Caps main-thread work during drag |
| Reorder prefs: update order array only; **do not** rerun width probe when only order changed | `computeCampaignListColumnWidths` is O(rows x cols) |
| Server pagination; client renders `items` page only | No `useMemo` filter over full dataset in browser |
| Row VM (`buildCampaignRowVm`) per body row | Parent filter/sort state does not reformat every cell string |
| Imperative `<col>` width during resize drag | `use_campaign_list_column_resize.ts` avoids React width state on `pointermove` |
| Virtualized tbody when row count > ~100 (future) | Constant DOM node count |

### VDOM reconcile scope (campaigns list; operator verified 2026-09)

Campaigns directory table (~35 visible columns, 100-row page) stays interactive on ingest-only dev stack after row VM + imperative resize landed. This is **not** windowed DOM virtualization yet; perf comes from narrowing React reconcile and layout work:

| Technique | File | Effect |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Row view-model | `campaign_list_row_vm.ts`, `campaign_list_table_body_row.tsx` | Derived labels/metrics computed once per row props change; cells render plain strings |
| Colgroup ref resize | `use_campaign_list_column_resize.ts` | Drag updates `<col style>` without `setState` each pixel |
| Header-local DnD highlight | `campaign_list_table_header_cell.tsx` | Avoids tbody re-render on every `dragover` |

Operator sign-off (2026-09): scroll, column resize, and filter refresh on full campaign page remain smooth; no main-thread stalls in DevTools during resize/drag.

Future: `@tanstack/react-virtual` or equivalent when page size exceeds ~100 rows without server pagination tightening.

### Anti-patterns (never; causes jank and main-thread block)

| Anti-pattern | What happens | Evidence in tree |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **`setState` on every `dragover` / `pointermove` in table root** | Full reconcile of header + **all body rows** on each event (10-60 Hz) | `campaigns_list_table.tsx` `setDragOverColumnId` on `onDragOver` |
| **Resize width via React state each pixel** | `setLocalWidths` -> re-render -> update every `<col style>` -> `table-layout: fixed` reflow on all cells | `use_campaign_list_column_resize.ts` `onPointerMove` |
| **Global `text-overflow: ellipsis` on all `th, td`** | Layout must measure clipped text on width change | Removed with BEM table blocks; use per-cell `whitespace-nowrap` where needed |
| **Row VM skipped** | Parent state reformats every metric cell on each render | `buildCampaignRowVm` in `campaign_list_table_body_row.tsx` |
| **No `memo` on body rows** | Any parent state change repaints every cell if VM inputs unchanged | Prefer row VM + narrow props; add `memo` when profiler shows idle tbody repaint |
| **Width recompute on column reorder** | Same numeric widths rescanned across all campaigns | `use_campaigns_directory_workspace.ts` `computedColumnWidths` deps on `visibleColumns` order |
| **Synchronous `localStorage` on drop** | `JSON.stringify` + write blocks drop frame | `saveCampaignListColumnPrefs` in `handleColumnDrop` |
| **HTML5 DnD on grip with React highlight in parent** | Extra `dragenter`/`dragleave` churn + browser drag image | `campaign_list_table_header_cell.tsx` |
| **Thousands of cells without virtualization** | Linear DOM cost magnifies any full-table render | ~35 cols x 100+ campaigns |

**Symptom:** visible lag / frozen UI while dragging column or resizing -- not network; **main-thread layout + React reconcile**, not JS byte copying.

### Column reorder (canonical flow)

1. Grip `onDragStart` -> `dataTransfer.setData(COLUMN_DRAG_MIME, columnId)` only; optional opacity on source header.
2. `onDragOver` -> `preventDefault()`; highlight target via **header-local** state or `data-drag-over` attribute.
3. `onDrop` -> `moveDataColumn(order, dragged, target)` -> persist prefs -> single React commit.
4. Body rows receive new `columns` array order; cells permute by `key={columnId}`.

Banned: calling `onColumnPrefsChange` / `saveCampaignListColumnPrefs` on `dragover`; re-fetching list on reorder.

### Column resize (canonical flow)

1. `pointerdown` on separator -> capture pointer; record `startX` / `startWidth`.
2. `pointermove` -> update **only** target `col` width (ref or CSS variable); optional rAF throttle.
3. `pointerup` -> `onColumnWidthCommit(columnId, widthPx)` once -> merge into prefs -> one React render.

Banned: spreading `{ ...widths, [id]: w }` into React state on every move event.

### Performance budget (directory tables)

Targets for campaigns-style directory tables (~35 columns, ~100 rows). Falsify in Chrome DevTools Performance before claiming "smooth" reorder/resize.

| Operation | Budget | Tool |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Column drag highlight | < 20 ms per `dragover` event | Performance panel (main thread) |
| Column resize move | < 16 ms per `pointermove` (60 fps) | Same |
| Table first paint (100 rows) | < 50 ms | Lighthouse or Performance trace |

Violations usually mean full-table React reconcile or `table-layout: fixed` reflow on every move -- see anti-patterns above.

### Verification (table performance claims)

| Claim | Falsify |
| :--- | :--- |
| "Reorder is smooth" | Performance panel: no long `Recalculate Style` / `Layout` stacks on `dragover` without drop; dragover handler < 20 ms |
| "Resize is smooth" | Same during `pointermove` < 16 ms; React profiler: body rows not re-rendering |
| "No full-table render on header interaction" | React DevTools highlight tbody on drag -- must stay idle until drop |

Reference files: `campaign_list_columns.ts` (`moveDataColumn`, `visibleCampaignListColumns`), `campaign_list_table_header_cell.tsx`, `use_campaign_list_column_resize.ts`, `campaign_list_table_body_row.tsx`, `campaign_list_column_widths.ts` (`computeCampaignListColumnWidths`).

### Fake promises (banned)

`useResource` and page fetchers must not simulate API success with in-memory stubs.

| Pattern | Verdict | Fix |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `if (!customerId) return Promise.resolve([])` | **Lie** -- UI shows empty table as if API returned `[]` | `return Promise.resolve(undefined)`; `hasSnapshot={data != null}`; show scope prompt / `EmptyState` |
| `return Promise.resolve({ items: [], total: 0 })` when guard fails | **Lie** | `undefined` + no snapshot |
| `return Promise.resolve(SEED_ROWS)` with non-empty array | **Lie** | Real `*_api.ts` against live control |
| `data ?? []` when `data` can be wrong-shaped object | **Lie** | Normalize in `*_api.ts` or fix mock; `Array.isArray` guard |

`Promise.resolve(undefined)` when a prerequisite is missing (no id, fetch disabled) is **OK**.

**Audit (2026-09):** `Promise.resolve([])` in scoped pages including `automation_rules_page.tsx`, `saved_views_page.tsx`, `fraud_integrations_page.tsx`, `report_schedules_page.tsx`, `telegram_postbacks_page.tsx`, `margin_guard_*_page.tsx`, `smart_alerts_*_page.tsx`, `brands_page.tsx`, `traffic_optimizer_rules_page.tsx`, `integrations_platform_campaigns_page.tsx`, `brand_creatives_page.tsx`. `selfserve_portal_page.tsx` uses `Promise.resolve({ invoices: [], total: 0 })`.

### Error handling (required; no silent recover)

Full catalog: **Explicit error handling vs error slop** (ES*/EC* explicit, EH-* slop). Summary:

| Surface | Required |
| :--- | :--- |
| `useResource` error | Pass `error` to `ErrorBlock`, `creativePanelError`, or directory `error` prop |
| `error && !hasSnapshot` | Full-page or section `ErrorBlock` -- not empty table |
| `error && hasSnapshot` | Stale snapshot + inline refresh error (see campaigns directory pattern) |
| API 501 / license | `StubBanner` with server message -- not blank main |
| Render throw | `AppErrorBoundary` is backstop only -- not a substitute for fetch error UI |
| `catch` in handlers | Surface toast or `ErrorBlock`; never `catch { setItems([]) }` |

Banned: silent `catch` to empty; rendering children without checking `error` when `hasSnapshot` is false; relying on Playwright `table.or(empty)` to hide `TypeError` overlays.

## Mock and API lie modes (never)

| Lie mode | What the agent implies | What is actually true | Falsify |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Fixture page** | "List loads from API" | `domains/` / `pages/` renders hardcoded rows without `*_api.ts` | Grep data source |
| **Resolved fake fetch** | "Hook fetches backend" | `Promise.resolve([])` or seed array on guard failure | See fake promises table |
| **Envelope vs array** | "API matches OpenAPI" | `{ items: [] }` vs bare `[]` | OpenAPI + live `curl` / L1 Playwright |
| **Catch-all 200** | "Empty state works" | Wrong envelope; `.map` crash | `emptyArray()` vs `emptyList()` |
| **Fake status** | "Save works" | `genericOk()` on mutations | Status + round-trip |
| **Mutation theater** | "Created" | POST 2xx but GET unchanged | POST then GET on live API |
| **Vite-only proof for T1** | "Ingest-only verified" | `npm run dev` without `:8188` healthy | T1+, `curl :8188/health` |
| **Silent chart KPIs** | "Dashboard shows API metrics" | Synthetic series without `chart_mock=1` | T1 empty API -> empty charts or labeled preview |
| **Demo rows as prod** | "Table populated" | Round KPIs without `StubBanner` | Server seed only on T1+ |
| **Incremental fixture ID** | `00000000-cust-...-000001`, `user_id: "buyer-1"` in e2e/fixtures | Fails seed parity | `seedDeterministicUuid` / `newRandomUuid`; **Entity IDs** |
| **Unrun UI gate** | "admin_web green" | No output | Paste command + exit code |

### Entity IDs (UUID contract)

**Operator mandate (2026-09):** wire `id` / `*_id` fields use **RFC 4122 UUID strings** (v4 runtime, v5 deterministic seed). Incremental counters (`000...001`, `buyer-1`, `padStart(12,'0')`) are slop in fixtures, handlers, and tests.

| Surface | Algorithm | Canonical implementation |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Production create | UUID v7 (preferred) or v4 | Go `uuid.NewV7()` / `uuid.New()` |
| DB seed row `n` (deterministic) | UUID v5 SHA-1 over namespace + `"kind:n"` | Go `seedDeterministicUUID` in `cmd/admin/seed_catalog.go` |
| E2E / fixture row `n` | Same v5 as DB seed when applicable | TS helpers aligned with Go seed tests |
| Runtime create in UI | UUID from server response | Client `newRandomUuid()` only for optimistic ids before 2xx if ever needed |
| Campaign `display_id` | Polynomial hash of UUID string | Go `CampaignDisplayID` |
| Ops / template slugs | Short string ids (`postgres`, `tpl-search`) | **Only** non-entity config keys -- never `customer_id` / `campaign_id` / `user_id` |

**Detection:** `isTrivialSequentialUuid` / `isPlaceholderSeedUuid` (`customer_label.ts`); Go `TestSeedCatalog_deterministicUUIDsAreRealistic`.

| Pattern | Example | Why |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Sequential UUID tail | `00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000041` | Load-test counter |
| Typed prefix + counter | `00000000-cust-4000-8000-000000000001` | Legacy `devUuid()` |
| `padStart` / `LPAD` uuid builder | `suffix.padStart(12, '0')` | Trivial increment |
| Slug as wire user id | `user_id: "buyer-1"`, `"user-1"` | OpenAPI UUID field |
| Integer as id | `id: 1`, `campaign_id: "42"` | Schema mismatch |
| Reused static id per POST | Same id on every wizard commit | Must use server response `id` after 2xx |

**Required when adding fixtures or seeds:**

1. Stable catalog rows: align with Go `seedDeterministicUUID` in `cmd/admin/seed_catalog.go`.
2. E2E creates: use server response UUID after POST -- not ad-hoc slug ids.
3. Foreign keys in fixtures: reference seeded rows -- not `buyer-1` style slugs.

## Test honesty taxonomy (Playwright E2E + domain unit)

**Runtime lies** (fake fetch, wrong wire shape) live in **Mock and API lie modes** above. This section defines **test lies**: green tests that do not prove what agents claim in PRs.

**Rule:** name **test type**, **tier** (T1-T2 from **Verification tiers**), and **proof level** (`L*`) in every PR test claim. Citing a green test without level is a lie.

### What each test type can prove

| Test type | Tier | Proves | Never proves |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `domains/**/*.test.ts` (pure) | -- | Formatting, column math, query string parse | API wiring, Go handler |
| `npm run dev` manual smoke | T1 | UX against live proxy to `:8188` | Handler unit coverage |
| Playwright @ `:8188` **L0-L1s** | T1/T2 stack | Route shell, login, heading, soft table/empty | Handler correctness, mutation persistence |
| Playwright **L1+** (`waitForResponse`) | T1/T2 | Live `/api/v1` read contract | Go unit coverage, CH rows |
| Playwright **L2+** | T1/T2 | Mutation HTTP round-trip visible in UI | Idempotency under retry, outbox |
| Go `*_handlers_test.go` / integration | Server | Handler + DB contract | React render |

**Banned citations:**

| Claim | Invalid sole evidence |
| :--- | :--- |
| "Go handler wired" | Playwright smoke, `smoke_matrix.spec.js`, pure domain unit tests |
| "OpenAPI parity shipped" | Client-only tests without live `/api/v1` |
| "E2E verified ingest-only" | Playwright without `curl :8188/health` and **L1+** network assert |
| "Mutation works" | `*_write.spec.js` that only opens a form |
| "List loads from API" | `table.or(empty).or(stub)` |

