## RBAC (server-authoritative; client UX only)

**Binding:** role and permission checks on **data access** live in Go (`control-plane.mdc` **RBAC**). The browser may hide nav links; it **must not** be the only gate. Media buyer (`MB`) and other scoped roles must get **no operator payload** when opening forbidden routes by URL.

### What the client may do (UX only)

| ID | Allowed | Purpose |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **RB-C1** | `filterNavItems` / `permissions.includes` on `nav_config.ts` | Hide sidebar and command palette entries |
| **RB-C2** | Disable buttons when `!permissions.includes('campaigns:write')` | Prevent pointless clicks; server still enforces on PATCH |
| **RB-C3** | `ErrorBlock` / `StubBanner` on `ApiError` status `403` | Operator-visible deny |
| **RB-C4** | Optional `<Navigate to="/forbidden" />` when route lacks permission | UX redirect only -- cite **RB-C4**; not security proof |

### Client RBAC slop (never ship)

| ID | Pattern | Example in tree | Required |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **RB-C5** | `user.role === 'MB'` (or any role string) as **sole** page gate | Future anti-pattern | Server `403` on every API for that page |
| **RB-C6** | `Promise.resolve([])` / empty table when fetch returns `403` | **EH-ST1** + RBAC leak fiction | **RB-C3** |
| **RB-C7** | `catch` on 403 -> navigate home silently | Operator blind | Show forbidden copy (`admin_error.ts`) |
| **RB-C8** | Client renders operator rows after `403` on primary GET | RBAC leak fiction | **RB-C3** `ErrorBlock`; empty table banned |
| **RB-C9** | E2E soft OR passes on `forbidden` text | `portals_smoke.spec.js` **FE2** | **L3** with `waitForResponse` 403 + alert |

