## Wire safety (cross-ref; server-owned)

JSON depth/size limits are enforced on the **Go handler**, not in browser mock code. Do not invent admin limits (e.g. 10 MiB / depth 100) in frontend docs -- cite repo constants.

| Surface | Limit | Source |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Admin `/api/v1` request bodies | 64 KiB default (`ReadLimitedBody` / `DecodeRequestOrBadRequest`) | `pkg/coldpath.DefaultMaxBody` (`cold-path.mdc`) |
| Track hot-path JSON parse | Max depth 16; max key pairs 10000 | `internal/ingest/parser/scan.go` (`parser.mdc`, `hot-path.mdc`) |
| OpenRTB JSON | Max depth 32 | same file |

**Gap (honest):** admin cold path uses stdlib `json.Unmarshal` without an explicit nesting-depth cap. Deep JSON bomb tests belong in `pkg/coldpath` / handler tests, not Playwright. Frontend: do not add custom recursive JSON parsers on API responses; use normal `fetch` + typed parse and surface `ErrorBlock` on non-2xx.

